# The two files that make data/ 11 GB instead of 648 MB.
#
# The expanded single-cell matrix is a build-time input: the loader goes
# through cache.ensure() and returns the cached group_means.npz whenever the
# fingerprint matches, so a service that never invalidates those fingerprints
# never opens it. The .gz beside it is the archive the matrix was expanded
# from and is redundant once it has been.
#
# This holds for ONE indication. The malignant-cells fingerprint includes a
# digest of the gene set, so a different cancer type produces a different pool,
# a cache miss, and this file back in the serving path. See specs/deployment.md.
data/singlecell/*.h5ad
data/singlecell/*.h5ad.gz

.venv/
.git/
.gitattributes
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Outputs, not inputs. The run report and the per-stage transcripts describe a
# run on the build machine and would be misleading inside the image.
reports/
run_all.py
make_artifact.py
verify_*.py
specs/
